#!/usr/bin/env node
// tools/validate-wellknown — AGSC-09-93. Checks one discovery document, served at
// /.well-known/knowledge-linkset, against AGSC-06-07…10, AGSC-06-08a, AGSC-06-35 and
// AGSC-11-16; with --peer, the mutual-conformance check of AGSC-10-12. Node stdlib
// only, zero dependencies, standalone (AGSC-09-90). Output: the AGSC-09-11 envelope
// under --json, one line per finding otherwise. Exit 0 pass, 1 fail, 2 usage.
//
//   validate-wellknown <url|file> [--level 0|1|2|3] [--peer <url|file>] [--json] [--dev]
//
// A <file> argument is a path to the document itself. Its targets are resolved on
// disk by mapping each same-origin href path onto the directory that contains
// `.well-known/` (a build output such as www/), so digests and surface targets
// are checked with no network (NFR-13).
//
// Error codes. The §9.4 registry names no dedicated code for the shape checks of
// AGSC-09-93 (DS-7 finding F1, 2026-09-17); until a MINOR assigns them this tool uses
// the most specific registered code under the precedence paragraph: AGSC-E201 for
// document shape, media type and order; AGSC-E202 for a REQUIRED attribute missing;
// AGSC-E204 for a malformed digest; AGSC-E209 for a relation outside AGSC-06-10/06-35;
// AGSC-E210 for a surface declaration that disagrees with the node; AGSC-E601 for
// non-canonical bytes at Level ≥ 2; AGSC-E901/E904/E905/E907 for I/O.
'use strict';
